AMA's knowledge base: one markdown document per topic, each with a `title` and a `min_level`
in its frontmatter. `knowledge_sync` reads every `.md` in this folder and `knowledge_search`
answers from it, which is why this placeholder is not markdown — anything with a `.md` suffix
here becomes a document AMA will quote. See "Knowledge" in docs/runbook.md, and
clients/demo-practice/knowledge for two worked examples. Empty for now: a search returns
nothing and AMA says she does not have it.
